    {
      "id": "Xref",
      "code_hash": "d7f8401c70a9630d1db33cd16890a145",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"analytic-inputs-and-normalization\">Analytic inputs and normalization</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Define <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(L_M=\\log M||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(L_{4\\pi}=\\log(4\\pi)||)</marimo-tex> in the reference's scale\nconvention. For its normalized integrals, the supplied poles are\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T^2=M^2\\left[\\frac1{\\epsilon^2}+\\frac{2(1-L_M)}{\\epsilon}\\right],\n\\qquad V=M\\left[\\frac{3}{2\\epsilon^2}+\\frac{9/2-3L_M}{\\epsilon}\\right].||)</marimo-tex>$\nEach loop restores <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(i(4\\pi)^{\\epsilon-2}||)</marimo-tex>. Keeping <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(d||)</marimo-tex> symbolic until after\nreduction retains the terms from <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(O(\\epsilon)||)</marimo-tex> coefficients times double poles.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The supplied one-loop insertion sum uses\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\delta Z_\\psi=-1/\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex>,\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\delta Z_A=\\delta Z_\\xi=-4N_f/(3\\epsilon)||)</marimo-tex>,\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\delta Z_e=2N_f/(3\\epsilon)||)</marimo-tex> and the auxiliary photon-mass counterterm\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\delta Z_{A m_{\\rm UV}}=-2N_f/\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex>.\nIn the same <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(i a_4^2\\not p||)</marimo-tex> units it is\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(-\\frac1{\\epsilon^2}+\n\\frac{4N_f/3+2/3-L_{4\\pi}+L_M}{\\epsilon}.||)</marimo-tex>$\nThe auxiliary-mass and normalization logarithms cancel against the generated\nbare result.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SFPL",
      "code_hash": "bb383a228843e19cd7fddf7b7a14290c",
